VulkanOptics (optics::)
======================

Reusable Vulkan material compositor and optional screen-space caustic
projection. The host owns rasterization, G-buffers, swapchain and command
buffers. VulkanOptics uses no hardware ray-tracing extensions.

Glass uses a pass-through, tint and mattness control. Reflective surfaces
use reflectivity and mattness. Screen-space reflection/refraction samples
the existing shaded opaque image when the reflected hit is visible.

When a reflected/refracted ray cannot resolve visible screen data, the
compositor queries the GPU stackless triangle BVH from VulkanPMap instead.
Off-screen hits are shaded using scene lights, material base colors and
the existing photon-grid indirect lighting. Matte off-screen reflections
use deterministic cone samples. No cubemap, static probe, approximate
environment fallback or separate acceleration structure is used.

The host supplies GPU geometry buffers through compositor::set_scene().
Keep the mapper and its GPU buffers alive until all referencing submissions
complete. Update descriptors only while the renderer is idle.

Caustic photons are projected into visible receiver depth, reconstructed
over a smooth finite footprint and filtered by the compositor. Photon
emission is cached until the scene/light/material changes; camera movement
does not rebuild the photon map.

Limitations: off-screen geometry currently uses per-face base color, not
the source mesh's sampled texture, and supports up to 16 point lights.
Software BVH reflections are workload-dependent and should be profiled
when mirror coverage is large.

Public API: optics/optics.hpp, optics/caustics.hpp.
Shaders: optics/shaders/*.frag, *.comp and raytrace.glsl.
